internal fun faqs(): List<Faq> = listOf(
Faq("هل أضع معجون الأسنان على الحرق؟","myth","لا. المعجون يحتبس الحرارة ويزيد خطر العدوى. بدلاً منه برّد الحرق بماء جارٍ فاتر 15 إلى 20 دقيقة ثم غطِّه بشاش نظيف.","p6"),
Faq("هل أضع الثلج مباشرة على الحرق؟","myth","لا. الثلج المباشر قد يضر الجلد أكثر. الماء الجاري الفاتر هو الأفضل.","p6"),
Faq("هل أُرجع رأس صاحب الرعاف للخلف؟","myth","لا. إرجاع الرأس يُنزل الدم للحلق والمعدة. أمِل الرأس للأمام قليلاً واضغط على الجزء الطري من الأنف 10 إلى 15 دقيقة.","p10"),
Faq("هل أضع ملعقة في فم من يصاب بنوبة تشنج؟","myth","لا أبداً. لن يبتلع لسانه، ووضع شيء في فمه قد يكسر أسنانه ويسد مجرى الهواء. أبعد الأشياء الخطرة وضع شيئاً لينّاً تحت رأسه.","p8"),
Faq("هل أشق مكان لدغة الأفعى وأمصّ السم؟","myth","لا. هذا يزيد تلف الأنسجة والمضاعفات. ثبّت الطرف واجعل المصاب هادئاً واتصل بالإسعاف.","p33"),
Faq("هل أسقي فاقد الوعي ماءً لينتبه؟","myth","لا. قد يختنق. ضعه في وضعية الإفاقة إن كان يتنفس، واتصل بالإسعاف.","p12"),
Faq("هل أضغط على بطن الغريق لإخراج الماء؟","myth","لا. هذا يؤخر الإنعاش ويسبب استنشاق القيء. ابدأ بالتنفس والضغطات الصدرية حسب الخطوات.","p17"),
Faq("هل أتوقف عن الإنعاش خوفاً من كسر الأضلاع؟","myth","لا. قد تنكسر الأضلاع أثناء الإنعاش الصحيح، لكن إنقاذ الحياة أهم. واصل الضغط حتى يصل المسعفون.","p3"),
Faq("هل أفك العاصبة بعد فترة لإراحة الطرف؟","myth","لا. فكّها يتم في المستشفى فقط. سجّل وقت التركيب وأبلغ به المسعفين.","p2"),
Faq("هل أعطي الأسبرين لكل من يشتكي من ألم الصدر؟","depends","ليس بقرار شخصي. اتصل بـ997 وأعطه أي دواء فقط إذا وجّهك موظف الطوارئ أو كان موصوفاً له. ولا يُعطى أبداً لمن يشتبه بجلطة دماغية.","p5"),
Faq("هل أحرّك مصاب الحادث بسرعة إلى سيارتي؟","myth","لا، إلا إذا كان في خطر مباشر كالحريق. التحريك الخاطئ قد يضر الرقبة والعمود الفقري.","p30"),
Faq("هل أعطي الطفل الأسبرين لخفض الحرارة؟","myth","لا. لا يُعطى الأسبرين للأطفال لخفض الحرارة. استشر 937 لجرعة خافض آمنة حسب الوزن.","p18"),
Faq("هل أسكب الماء على حريق زيت المقلاة؟","myth","لا. الماء يطلق كرات من النار في المطبخ. أطفئ المصدر وغطِّ المقلاة بغطاء معدني أو بطانية حريق.","p21"),
Faq("هل يجوز الفطر لمن ظهرت عليه علامات هبوط السكر في رمضان؟","true","نعم، فالحفاظ على النفس مقدّم، ويُفطر ثم يعالج الهبوط. واسأل أهل العلم عن القضاء، وراجع طبيبك قبل الصيام.","p45"),
Faq("هل أقف عند الجدار لأرتاح في الزحام الشديد؟","myth","لا. الجدران والحواجز أشد مواضع الضغط. اتجه مبكراً للحافة أو مخرج جانبي وابقَ واقفاً وذراعاك أمام صدرك.","p44")
)
internal fun enCards(): Map<String,EnCard> = mapOf(
"p1" to EnCard("Choking in adults and children over 1 year (Heimlich maneuver)","Critical medical emergency: act within seconds","If the person is coughing forcefully or can speak: do not press on their abdomen. Encourage them to keep coughing. Step in only if they cannot breathe or make a sound.",listOf("Stand directly behind the person, wrap your arms around their waist, and lean their upper body slightly forward.","Make a fist with one hand and place it just above the navel, about two fingers wide, below the breastbone.","Grasp your fist with your other hand and give quick, firm thrusts inward and upward (a J-shaped motion).","Repeat the thrusts (5 times in a row) until the object comes out or normal breathing returns.","If the person becomes unconscious: lower them gently to the ground, call 997, and start CPR."),listOf("Do not give water or any liquid during choking.","Do not blindly put your fingers in the mouth.","Do not use abdominal thrusts on pregnant or very obese people (use chest thrusts in the center of the chest).")),
"p2" to EnCard("Severe arterial bleeding (tourniquet and wound packing)","Extremely critical: stopping the bleeding is the top priority","Lost blood cannot be replaced in the field. Press hard and steadily from the first second, and do not lift the gauze to check whether the bleeding has stopped.",listOf("Expose the wound quickly to find the real source of bleeding, and ask someone to call 997 right away.","For severe bleeding in an arm or leg, place a tourniquet 5 to 7 cm above the wound (not directly over a joint).","Tighten the tourniquet firmly until the bleeding stops completely and the pulse below it disappears, then lock the strap in the clip.","Write the exact time the tourniquet was applied on the strap or on the person's forehead (use the timer in this app).","For deep wounds where a tourniquet cannot be used (neck, armpit, groin): pack the wound with sterile gauze and keep firm, direct pressure with both hands for 3 to 5 full minutes."),listOf("Never loosen or remove a tourniquet once applied; only the hospital medical team does that.","Do not remove blood-soaked gauze; add new layers on top and keep pressing.","Do not place a tourniquet directly over the knee or elbow, or over pockets with hard objects.")),
"p3" to EnCard("Adult CPR (cardiopulmonary resuscitation)","Extremely critical: every second counts","Push hard and fast in the center of the chest (100 to 120 compressions per minute), 5 to 6 cm deep, and let the chest fully recoil after each compression.",listOf("Make sure the scene is safe, shake the person's shoulders, shout \"Can you hear me?\", and check breathing for no more than 10 seconds.","If there is no response and no normal breathing: ask someone to call 997 immediately and bring an automated external defibrillator (AED) if available.","Lay the person on their back on a firm surface. Place the heel of one hand in the center of the chest (lower half of the breastbone) and interlock your other hand on top.","Keep your arms straight and push down with your body weight at about 110 compressions per minute (you can use the rhythm tool in this app).","Continue without stopping until breathing returns, the Red Crescent team arrives, or an AED is available."),listOf("Never pause chest compressions for more than 10 seconds.","Do not bend your elbows while pressing, and do not press on the side ribs or the lower tip of the breastbone.","Do not leave the person alone to look for help if you have a phone; put it on speaker.")),
"p4" to EnCard("Severe allergic reaction (anaphylaxis)","Critical medical emergency: airway at risk","If a skin allergy comes with difficulty breathing, a hoarse voice, swelling of the tongue or throat, or severe dizziness, it is anaphylaxis and needs an epinephrine auto-injector (EpiPen) and an ambulance immediately.",listOf("Call the Red Crescent (997) at once and say you suspect a severe allergic reaction.","If the person has their own epinephrine auto-injector (EpiPen): remove the blue safety cap and inject straight into the middle of the outer thigh (it can go through clothing), holding it in place for 3 to 10 seconds.","Lay the person on their back with legs raised, or let them sit if they have severe shortness of breath.","Loosen tight clothing around the neck and chest, and keep checking breathing and consciousness.","If symptoms do not improve, follow the emergency operator's guidance about a second dose if another pen is available."),listOf("Do not rely on antihistamine tablets alone when the throat is swelling or breathing is difficult; they work too slowly.","Do not let the person stand up suddenly during a reaction.","Do not inject the pen into a vein, fingers or buttocks; the only safe place is the outer thigh muscle.")),
"p5" to EnCard("Suspected heart attack or stroke (FAST)","Critical: time saves the brain and the heart","For a suspected stroke: note the exact minute the first symptom appeared. Clot-dissolving treatment depends entirely on the time since symptoms began.",listOf("For stroke, use FAST: ask the person to smile (is the mouth drooping?), raise both arms (does one drop?), and say a simple sentence (is the speech slurred?).","For a heart attack: watch for chest pain or crushing pressure that spreads to the left arm, jaw or back, with cold sweat and nausea.","Call 997 immediately; do not wait for the symptoms to pass.","Help the person sit half upright and comfortable (back supported, knees slightly bent) to reduce strain on the heart, and keep them calm.","Do not give any medication (including aspirin) unless the emergency operator tells you to or it was prescribed to them, and stay with them until the ambulance arrives."),listOf("Do not give a suspected stroke patient any medication (including aspirin), food or drink: a stroke may be caused by bleeding and swallowing may be impaired.","Do not let the person walk, exert themselves, or drive to the hospital.")),
"p14" to EnCard("Choking in an infant (under 1 year)","Extremely critical: special infant protocol","For infants under 1 year, never press on the abdomen (no abdominal Heimlich) because of the risk of liver injury; use 5 back blows + 5 chest thrusts.",listOf("Place the infant face down along your forearm, supporting the jaw and head with your hand without covering the mouth, with the head lower than the body.","Give 5 firm blows with the heel of your other hand in the middle of the back, between the shoulder blades.","If the object does not come out: carefully turn the infant onto their back along your other forearm, keeping the head lower.","Place two fingers in the center of the chest just below the nipple line and give 5 quick chest thrusts about 4 cm deep.","Keep alternating 5 back blows and 5 chest thrusts while calling 997, until the object comes out and the infant cries or breathes."),listOf("Never press on the abdomen of an infant under one year.","Do not hold the infant by the feet upside down or shake them hard.")),
"p20" to EnCard("Home gas leak (LPG)","Explosion and fire risk: evacuate and secure immediately","If you smell gas, do not touch any electrical switch (do not turn any light or extractor fan on or off); a tiny internal spark can cause an explosion.",listOf("Close the main gas cylinder valve and the stove knobs right away if it is safe to reach them.","Quietly open all windows and outside doors to ventilate the home and disperse gas that collects near the floor.","Evacuate everyone from the home immediately (use the stairs, never the elevator).","Switch off the electricity at the main breaker only if the breaker box is outside the home and away from the leak.","Once in a safe place, call Civil Defense on 998 if the leak continues."),listOf("Do not turn on an extractor fan, switch lights off, or unplug anything inside the suspected area.","Never test for a leak with a lighter or match.")),
"p21" to EnCard("Kitchen, cooking-oil and electrical fires (PASS method)","Fire and smoke spreading: act or evacuate immediately","Never pour water on a burning pan of oil; the water turns to steam instantly and throws burning drops across the kitchen.",listOf("Oil pan fire: turn off the gas or power, cover the pan tightly with a fire blanket or a metal lid to cut off oxygen, and leave it until fully cool.","Appliance fire: cut the power at the main breaker first, then use a dry powder (ABC) or CO2 extinguisher.","To use an extinguisher, follow PASS: Pull the pin, Aim at the base of the flames, Squeeze the handle, Sweep side to side.","If the fire is large or the smoke is heavy: close the door of the burning room behind you to contain it and leave the home at once.","When escaping through smoke, stay low and cover your nose and mouth with a wet cloth, then call Civil Defense (998)."),listOf("Do not carry a burning oil pan to the sink or outside; the burning oil will spill on you.","Never use the elevator during a fire."))
)
